==============================================================================
eFEDS ALONE: S in radial bands.  This is the only internal radial
information any survey here has.
==============================================================================
   r/R500  0.50- 0.80  n=   99  median x=  0.69  S =  1.820 [ 1.429,  2.213]  median M_gas500 = 6.57e+12
   r/R500  0.80- 1.30  n=  361  median x=  1.07  S =  1.303 [ 1.122,  1.496]  median M_gas500 = 5.47e+12
   r/R500  1.30- 2.00  n=  569  median x=  1.65  S =  1.230 [ 1.084,  1.380]  median M_gas500 = 6.02e+12
   r/R500  2.00- 3.20  n=  787  median x=  2.55  S =  1.230 [ 1.109,  1.334]  median M_gas500 = 6.44e+12
   r/R500  3.20- 5.00  n=  758  median x=  4.00  S =  0.741 [ 0.631,  0.851]  median M_gas500 = 6.96e+12
   r/R500  5.00- 8.00  n=  645  median x=  6.12  S =  0.668 [ 0.543,  0.804]  median M_gas500 = 4.76e+12
   r/R500  8.00-35.00  n=  139  median x= 10.00  S =  0.355 [ 0.100,  0.708]  median M_gas500 = 6.59e+11

   eFEDS internal radial slope  beta = -0.4102 +- 0.0968   (weighted fit to the 7 bands above)
   For comparison, a PURE radius story joining eFEDS at r/R500 ~ 2.5 to the
   strong-lens cores at ~0.1 needs beta = -0.7937.

==============================================================================
IS THE eFEDS INTERNAL RADIAL SLOPE REAL?  three checks
==============================================================================
   1. declared train/held split (the closure lane's, by sorted id)
      TRAIN beta = -0.5229 +- 0.1278 (7 bands)
      HELD  beta = -0.3620 +- 0.1452 (7 bands)
      difference -0.1609 +- 0.1934  ->  -0.8 sigma

   2. r/R500 < 3.2 only, where the Vikhlinin fit is not far extrapolated
      beta = -0.1897 +- 0.1466 (4 bands)

   3. the SAME statistic on the B-mode (cross) component, which must be flat
      beta = -0.0691 +- 0.1626 (7 bands)

==============================================================================
MATCHED-RADIUS COMPARISON 2: eFEDS vs LoCuSS at r/R500 ~ 1
==============================================================================
   eFEDS  r/R500 0.8-1.3, n = 361, median M_gas500 = 5.47e+12:  S = 1.303 [1.122, 1.496]
   LoCuSS r/R500 = 1 exactly, n = 27, median M_gas500 = 9.86e+13:  S = 1.689 +- 0.061 in ln
   mass ratio 18.0x at the SAME radius  ->  ln S difference +0.259 (+1.7 sigma)
   implied alpha = +0.0897

   *** The two matched-radius comparisons DISAGREE: alpha = +0.397
   from eFEDS-vs-SL at r/R500 ~ 0.5, but +0.090 from eFEDS-vs-LoCuSS at
   r/R500 ~ 1, over comparable mass ratios (25x and 18x).
   A single mass power law cannot produce both.

==============================================================================
STRONG-LENS CLUSTERS: their OWN internal radial slope, at fixed
mass, from many image systems in one cluster
==============================================================================
   A2744      n=22  ln r span 2.80  beta = +0.1648 +- 0.0277
   AS1063     n=10  ln r range only 0.60 -- too narrow, skipped
   MACSJ0717  n= 8  ln r span 1.38  beta = +0.4269 +- 0.0596
   MACSJ1149  n= 9  ln r span 1.24  beta = -0.4970 +- 0.2530
   combined  beta = +0.2045 +- 0.0250   (eFEDS internal: -0.4102 +- 0.0968)


